1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,690
By now, most of us will have heard of GMOs.
到目前为止，我们大多数人都听说过转基因生物（GMOs）。

2
00:00:05,690 --> 00:00:12,220
In case you haven't, GMO stands for genetically-modified organism.
如果你还不了解，GMO是“genetically-modified organism”的缩写，即转基因生物。

3
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:21,040
This basically means that an organism has had a foreign genetic sequence introduced into it.
这本质上意味着一种生物被植入了外来基因序列。

4
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:36,940
In theory, this gives the organism certain advantages – it may become hardier by developing a resistance to disease, or in the case of GM food, may be bigger and require fewer nutrients to develop.
理论上，这会赋予该生物某些优势——它可能通过产生抗病性变得更顽强，而就转基因食品而言，它可能会更大，且生长所需的营养更少。

5
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:41,300
GM organisms have been used for a while.
转基因生物的应用已有一段时间了。

6
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:51,690
Scientists in the UK are trialling a GM wheat which allegedly yields 40% more crop in greenhouse conditions.
英国科学家正在试验一种转基因小麦，据称在温室条件下其产量能提高40%。

7
00:00:51,690 --> 00:01:05,710
GM hens, which are able to lay eggs from different poultry breeds, have been used by scientists in Edinburgh to conserve rare birds by storing their stem cells in a seed bank.
爱丁堡的科学家利用转基因母鸡（这种母鸡能产下不同家禽品种的鸡蛋），将稀有鸟类的干细胞储存在种子库中，以保护这些珍稀物种。

8
00:01:05,710 --> 00:01:20,210
And more recently, scientists in China used information from the genome of a plant to increase the production of a key malaria drug, helping to meet the large global demand.
最近，中国科学家利用一种植物的基因组信息，提高了一种关键抗疟药物的产量，助力满足全球的巨大需求。

9
00:01:20,210 --> 00:01:35,060
But now scientists at the University of Edinburgh's Roslin Institute have created GE pigs which are allegedly immune to one of the world's costliest livestock diseases.
但如今，爱丁堡大学罗斯林研究所的科学家们培育出了基因编辑（GE）猪，据称这种猪对全球代价最大的家畜疾病之一具有免疫力。

10
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:38,890
GE stands for gene editing.
GE是“gene editing”的缩写，即基因编辑。

11
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:44,910
Unlike GM, gene editing merely alters the DNA of the creature.
与仅对生物的DNA进行修饰的转基因不同。

12
00:01:44,910 --> 00:01:59,220
In this case, a small region of pig DNA was deleted, preventing contraction of the PRRS virus, or Porcine Reproductive and Respiratory Syndrome virus.
在这个案例中，研究人员删除了猪DNA中的一个小片段，使其能够抵抗猪繁殖与呼吸综合征病毒（PRRS病毒）。

13
00:01:59,220 --> 00:02:08,640
The virus causes breathing problems and death, but even after the GE pigs were exposed to it, none have become ill.
这种病毒会导致呼吸问题甚至死亡，但即使基因编辑猪接触到该病毒，也没有出现发病情况。

14
00:02:08,640 --> 00:02:15,980
And the effect is permanent, so the resistance will be passed on through natural breeding.
而且这种效果是永久性的，因此抗病性会通过自然繁殖传递给后代。

15
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:26,830
Tests so far showed that the animals are not weakened in any other way by the process, claims Research leader Dr Christine Tait-Burkard.
研究负责人克里斯汀·泰特-伯卡德博士表示，迄今为止的测试表明，这一过程没有以任何其他方式影响这些动物的健康。

16
00:02:26,830 --> 00:02:35,870
"The main thing that this edit will do is benefit animal welfare because the animals will not get a devastating disease."
“这种基因编辑的主要作用是改善动物福利，因为这些动物不会再感染这种毁灭性的疾病。”

17
00:02:35,870 --> 00:02:42,800
However, critics have argued that the creature's welfare will actually suffer because of this.
然而，批评者认为，这种做法实际上会损害动物。

18
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:51,470
Helen Browning of the Soil Association believes this only addresses the symptom of the problem and not the root cause.
土壤协会的海伦·布朗宁认为，这只是治标不治本。

19
00:02:51,470 --> 00:03:00,120
"It is not encouraging companies to change the way they keep their pigs so they don't become diseased in the first place", she says.
“它并没有鼓励企业改变养猪方式，从源头上避免猪患病，”她说。

20
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:09,480
Regardless, this is an experiment and while the technique appears to work, it is several years away from regulation and implementation.
尽管如此，这仍处于实验阶段。

21
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:19,790
“On top of that, only if these studies are successful and the public are accepting, would we integrate these gene edits into commercial breeding stocks,"
虽然该技术看似有效，但距离监管批准和实际应用还需要数年时间。

22
00:03:19,790 --> 00:03:22,710
Dr Tait-Burkard told the BBC.
泰特-伯卡德博士告诉英国广播公司：“此外，只有当这些研究取得成功且获得公众认可时，我们才会将这些基因编辑技术应用到商业育种中。”

23
00:03:22,710 --> 00:03:26,120
So it seems we may have a while yet.
因此，看来我们还需要等待一段时间。
